#X text 46 22 By default \, the contents of [dict] are not saved as part of the patch \, but you can change that with the "-k" (short for 'keep') flag. You can also change this status with the 'keep' message \, and it will remains valid when reopening and resaving the patch., f 44;
#X text 46 96 Note that changing the data is not enough \, you have to save the patch! If you have 'keep' enabled \, the patch asks you to save if contents changed anyway., f 44;
